1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:06,692
This video shows you how to run workers that grow and shrink with load,

2
00:00:06,692 --> 00:00:09,790
each pod enrolling itself when it starts.

3
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:17,367
Open a new file, smeltr-worker-ingest.yaml, and paste in the guide's autoscaled manifest.

4
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:25,030
These workers join the ingest group.

5
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:29,015
As before, change the leader's address to yours.

6
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:33,562
This secret holds the enrollment code.

7
00:00:33,562 --> 00:00:35,161
Mint one now.

8
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:43,940
In Enrollment codes, add a code for the ingest group.

9
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:46,950
This time it brings in ephemeral workers.

10
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,426
The autoscaler starts and removes pods all the time.

11
00:00:50,426 --> 00:00:53,983
The leader forgets an ephemeral worker once it's gone,

12
00:00:53,983 --> 00:00:57,390
so removed pods don't pile up as silent workers.

13
00:00:57,440 --> 00:01:00,816
The autoscaler decides how many pods there are,

14
00:01:00,816 --> 00:01:04,263
so an ephemeral code has no limit and no expiry.

15
00:01:04,263 --> 00:01:06,490
It works until you withdraw it.

16
00:01:06,490 --> 00:01:08,190
Mint it, and copy it.

17
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:12,672
Back in the terminal, paste the ephemeral code into the secret.

18
00:01:14,760 --> 00:01:19,710
The workers run as a deployment, so any pod can be replaced by another.

19
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:26,136
Name the image by the same digest as the leader's, read in from digest.txt.

20
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:33,270
Each pod keeps its identity in an empty dir, so it lives and dies with the pod.

21
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:36,440
The autoscaler keeps between two and twelve pods.

22
00:01:36,440 --> 00:01:41,790
It adds pods when they average more than seventy percent of the CPU they request.

23
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:43,750
Save the file.

24
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:44,574
Apply it.

25
00:01:44,574 --> 00:01:49,903
The code's secret stays: every new pod enrolls with it.

26
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:03,750
In Status, the ingest group has two workers, both online.

27
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:07,198
Delete one of the pods, as a scale-down would.

28
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:21,040
The stopped worker told the leader it was going, and the leader forgot it at once.

29
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:23,550
The new pod enrolled as a new worker.

30
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:25,498
Check on learning.

31
00:02:25,698 --> 00:02:30,805
Why does the autoscaled manifest keep the enrollment code's secret?

32
00:02:35,205 --> 00:02:39,173
Every new pod enrolls with it, as a new worker.

33
00:02:40,073 --> 00:02:42,016
That's Install on Kubernetes.

34
00:02:42,016 --> 00:02:48,647
You ran the leader, added a worker that keeps its identity, and autoscaled a worker group.
